"id":"hippo_rag","label":"HippoRAG"},{"id":"iterative_retrieval_method","label":"iterative retrieval methods"},{"id":"online_retrieval_efficiency","label":"online retrieval efficiency"},{"id":"single_step_multi_hop_retrieval","label":"single-step multi-hop retrieval"}]},{"citationId":"c39","pages":[{"id":"hippo_rag","label":"HippoRAG"}]},{"citationId":"c40","pages":[{"id":"hippo_rag","label":"HippoRAG"},{"id":"mu_si_que","label":"MuSiQue"},{"id":"personalized_page_rank","label":"Personalized PageRank"}]}],"mentions":[{"citationId":"c8"},{"citationId":"c41"},{"citationId":"c42"},{"citationId":"c14"},{"citationId":"c25"},{"citationId":"c28"},{"citationId":"c43"},{"citationId":"c33"},{"citationId":"c44"},{"citationId":"c45"}],"mentionsLeftOut":40,"citations":[{"id":"c1","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_784801446a75a137","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":1,"quote":"In this work, we introduce HippoRAG, a novel retrieval framework inspired by the hippocampal indexing theory of human long-term memory to enable deeper and more efficient knowledge integration over new experiences."},{"id":"c2","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_04dddb1c2d05d742","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":25,"quote":"Idelalisib F Error Analysis F.1 Overview In this section, we provide a detailed error analysis of 100 errors made by HippoRAG on the MuSiQue dataset."},{"id":"c3","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_25925dce380bac5b","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":28,"quote":"Specifically, as seen in Table 17, retrieval costs for IRCoT are 10 to 30 times higher than HippoRAG since it only requires extracting relevant named entities from the query instead of processing all of the retrieved documents."},{"id":"c4","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_15160cee505e4ff0","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":8,"quote":"MuSiQue 2Wiki HotpotQA Average AR@2 AR@5 AR@2 AR@5 AR@2 AR@5 AR@2 AR@5 ColBERTv2 [70] 6.8 16.1 25.1 37.1 33.3 59.0 21.7 37.4 HippoRAG 10.2 22.4 45.4 75.7 33.8 57.9 29.8 52.0 We further illustrate HippoRAG’s unique single-step multi-hop"},{"id":"c5","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_6450d43634bcc2d0","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":2,"quote":"Given a new query, HippoRAG identifies the key concepts in the query and runs the Personalized PageRank (PPR) algorithm [30] on the KG, using the query concepts as the seeds, to integrate information across passages for retrieval."},{"id":"c6","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_1561f63effe8dae8","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":5,"quote":"HippoRAG outperforms all baselines on MuSiQue and 2WikiMultiHopQA and achieves comparable performance on the less challenging HotpotQA dataset."},{"id":"c7","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_52db994c3f719089","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":9,"quote":"In contrast, HippoRAG can continuously integrate new knowledge by simply adding edges to its KG."},{"id":"c8","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_784801446a75a137","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":1,"quote":"HippoRAG: Neurobiologically Inspired Long-Term Memory for Large Language Models Bernal Jiménez Gutiérrez The Ohio State University Yiheng Shu The Ohio State University Yu Gu The Ohio State University Michihiro Yasunaga Stanford University"},{"id":"c9","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_38b152c9607dfd2e","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":6,"quote":"44.7 61.2 75.6 65.6 79.0 53.7 66.4 IRCoT + Contriever 39.1 52.2 51.6 63.8 65.9 81.6 52.2 65.9 IRCoT + ColBERTv2 41.7 53.7 64.1 74.4 67.9 82.0 57.9 70.0 IRCoT + HippoRAG (Contriever) 43.9 56.6 75.3 93.4 65.8 82.3 61.7 77.4 IRCoT + HippoRAG"},{"id":"c10","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_1cae4879d57c3f3a","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":8,"quote":"5.2 HippoRAG’s Advantage: Single-Step Multi-Hop Retrieval A major advantage of HippoRAG over conventional RAG methods in multi-hop QA is its ability to perform multi-hop retrieval in a single step."},{"id":"c11","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_5a03cbc1c12462e6","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":10,"quote":"Like these works, HippoRAG shows the potential for synergy between these two technologies, combining the knowledge graph construction abilities of LLMs with the retrieval advantages of structured knowledge for more effective RAG."},{"id":"c12","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_77febadcd6c2ca2b","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":9,"quote":"Some other methods, such as RAPTOR [71], MemWalker [9] and GraphRAG [18], integrate infor- mation during the offline indexing phase similarly to HippoRAG and might be able to handle these more complex tasks."},{"id":"c13","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_048c301c94c7b71d","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":10,"quote":"Additionally, as shown in Appendix F.4, more work must be done to improve the consistency of OpenIE in longer compared to shorter documents. Finally, and perhaps most importantly, HippoRAG’s scalability still calls for further validation."},{"id":"c14","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_26123cbf6c0c09ef","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":1,"quote":"s complex, 1Code and data are available at https://github.com/OSU-NLP-Group/HippoRAG."},{"id":"c15","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_a34fa5fef80d4cb7","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":6,"quote":"For multi-step or iterative retrieval, our experiments in Table 3 demonstrate that IRCoT [78] and HippoRAG are complementary."},{"id":"c16","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_a34fa5fef80d4cb7","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":6,"quote":"As seen in Table 2, HippoRAG outperforms all other methods, including recent LLM-augmented baselines such as Propositionizer and RAPTOR, on our main datasets, MuSiQue and 2WikiMultiHopQA, while achieving competitive performance on HotpotQA."},{"id":"c17","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_8240c2e11040036d","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":26,"quote":"Since the only concept tagged by HippoRAG is “protons”, it extracts passages related to “Uranium” and “nuclear weapons” while ColBERTv2 uses the context to extract more relevant passages associated with the discovery of atomic numbers."},{"id":"c18","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_b6219633c5101433","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":7,"quote":"MuSiQue 2Wiki HotpotQA Average R@2 R@5 R@2 R@5 R@2 R@5 R@2 R@5 HippoRAG 40.9 51.9 70.7 89.1 60.5 77.7 57.4 72.9 OpenIE Alternatives REBEL [34] 31.7 39.6 63.1 76.5 43.9 59.2 46.2 58.4 Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct [1] 40.8 51.9 62.5 77.5 59.9 75.1"},{"id":"c19","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_5a59c3b07af14c98","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":24,"quote":"While HippoRAG is able to leverage the associations within the supporting passages to identify the Chlorambucil passage as the most important, ColBERTv2 and IRCoT are only able to extract passages associated with lymphocytic leukemia."},{"id":"c20","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_f248eb3ec470321e","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":10,"quote":"HippoRAG’s knowledge integration capabilities, demonstrated by its strong results on path-following multi-hop QA and promise on path-finding multi-hop QA, as well as its dramatic efficiency improvements and continuously updating nature,"},{"id":"c21","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_8418f7296aeb1d6a","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":1,"quote":"We compare HippoRAG with existing RAG methods on multi-hop question answering (QA) and show that our method outperforms the state-of-the-art methods remarkably, by up to 20%."},{"id":"c22","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_15406a6ab39fd7df","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":25,"quote":"Table 10: Ranking result examples for different approaches on several path-finding multi-hop questions. Question HippoRAG ColBERTv2 IRCoT Which book was published in 2012 by an English author who is a Whitbread Award winner?"},{"id":"c23","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_e48772351a996bb8","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":8,"quote":".1 25.1 37.1 33.3 59.0 21.7 37.4 HippoRAG 10.2 22.4 45.4 75.7 33.8 57.9 29.8 52.0 We further illustrate HippoRAG’s unique single-step multi-hop retrieval ability through the first example in Table 7."},{"id":"c24","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_4eb522b69751bf59","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":24,"quote":"E.2 Qualitative Analysis In Table 10, we show three more examples from three different domains that illustrate HippoRAG’s potential for solving retrieval tasks that require such cross-passage knowledge integration."},{"id":"c25","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_46510d19e232344a","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":2,"quote":"Inspired by this mechanism, HippoRAG allows LLMs to build and leverage a similar graph of associations to tackle knowledge integration tasks."},{"id":"c26","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_a3afbe5e19462e1a","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":20,"quote":"A HippoRAG Pipeline Example To better demonstrate how our HippoRAG pipeline works, we use the path-following example from the MuSiQue dataset shown in Table 7."},{"id":"c27","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_6bc91e5970bf1a0e","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":7,"quote":"7 45.7 59.2 38.4 51.7 Question Answering Results. We report QA results for HippoRAG, the strongest retrieval baselines, ColBERTv2 and IRCoT, as well as IRCoT using HippoRAG as a retriever in Table 4."},{"id":"c28","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_6450d43634bcc2d0","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":2,"quote":"In this work, we propose HippoRAG, a RAG framework that serves as a long-term memory for LLMs by mimicking this model of human memory."},{"id":"c29","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_91d69c7850715a51","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":29,"quote":"We combine IRCoT with different retrievers by replacing its base retriever BM25 with each retrieval method, including HippoRAG, noted as “IRCoT + HippoRAG” below.8 For the QA reader, we use top-5 retrieved passages as the context and"},{"id":"c30","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_97a2c1929ff7918a","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":6,"quote":"We report QA results for HippoRAG, the strongest retrieval baselines, ColBERTv2 and IRCoT, as well as IRCoT using HippoRAG as a retriever in Table 4."},{"id":"c31","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_25925dce380bac5b","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":28,"quote":"of HippoRAG’s main advantages against iterative retrieval methods is the dramatic online retrieval efficiency gains brought on by its single-step multi-hop retrieval ability in terms of both cost and time."},{"id":"c32","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_e48772351a996bb8","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":8,"quote":"In this example, even though Alhandra was not mentioned in Vila de Xira’s passage, HippoRAG can directly leverage Vila de Xira’s connection to Alhandra as his place of birth to determine its importance, something that standard RAG methods"},{"id":"c33","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_f4893ab658d98bee","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":2,"quote":"2 HippoRAG In this section, we first give a brief overview of the hippocampal memory indexing theory, followed by how HippoRAG’s indexing and retrieval design was inspired by this theory, and finally offer a more detailed account of our"},{"id":"c34","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_0b6893e7d9b607d7","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":4,"quote":"\" # $ % ( , !) Figure 2: Detailed HippoRAG Methodology. We model the three components of human long-term memory to mimic its pattern separation and completion functions."},{"id":"c35","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_97a2c1929ff7918a","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":6,"quote":"For multi-step or iterative retrieval, our experiments in Table 3 demonstrate that IRCoT [78] and HippoRAG are complementary."},{"id":"c36","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_048c301c94c7b71d","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":10,"quote":"Finally, and perhaps most importantly, HippoRAG’s scalability still calls for further validation."},{"id":"c37","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_15160cee505e4ff0","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":8,"quote":"We measure the percentage of queries for which all supporting passages are successfully retrieved (all-recall, denoted as AR@2 or AR@5) and find even larger performance improvements for HippoRAG."},{"id":"c38","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_25925dce380bac5b","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":28,"quote":"Also as seen in Table 17, HippoRAG can be 6 to 13 times faster than IRCoT, depending on the number of retrieval rounds that need to be executed (2-4 in our experiments).6 Table 17: Average cost and efficiency measurements for online"},{"id":"c39","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_38b152c9607dfd2e","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":6,"quote":"Generally, we find that HippoRAG’s performance is rather robust to its hyperparameters."},{"id":"c40","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_38b152c9607dfd2e","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":6,"quote":"We use 100 examples from MuSiQue’s training data to tune HippoRAG’s two hyperparameters: the synonymy threshold τ at 0.8 and the PPR damping factor at 0.5, which determines the probability that PPR will restart a random walk from the query"},{"id":"c41","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_8418f7296aeb1d6a","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":1,"quote":"HippoRAG synergistically orchestrates LLMs, knowledge graphs, and the Personalized PageRank algorithm to mimic the different roles of neocortex and hippocampus in human memory."},{"id":"c42","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_c26f4958a3b01964","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":1,"quote":"Although less complex, 1Code and data are available at https://github.com/OSU-NLP-Group/HippoRAG."},{"id":"c43","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_c80149a827872cde","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":2,"quote":"PPR enables HippoRAG to explore KG paths and identify relevant subgraphs, essentially performing multi-hop reasoning in a single retrieval step."},{"id":"c44","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_159eef9c90ddac14","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":3,"quote":"2.2 Overview Our proposed approach, HippoRAG, is closely inspired by the process described above."},{"id":"c45","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_7e3ed7593eeafe4f","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":